yaml/tag
description: A !tag before a value - names its type explicitly
- >
  A **tag** before a value names its type instead of letting the plain-scalar rules resolve
  it - `!!str`, `!!int` and kin from the core schema, or an application's own `!name`:
- !!<format: text/x-yaml> |
  version: !!str 1.2
  point: !point {x: 1, y: 2}
